# 2026-11-01 — research/vps-2026-11-01

- branch: `research/vps-2026-11-01`
- cycles run: 1 (cycle 64: Track 2 hybrid-trailer-hostile mirror-split micro-step)
- files tested: 2 synthetic appended-revision PDFs (aes256_r6__plain, rc4_128_r4__plain + injected page + hostile `/Encrypt` in classic trailer + ORIGINAL `/Encrypt` ref in XRefStm), no-password probes only

## Probe counts

- t_hostileTrailer_origXS (Track 2, cycle 64): NEW variant, mirror split of cycle 63 (classic trailer carries the cycle-33 V5/R6 hostile DIRECT dict — zeroed O/U/OE/UE, zeroed Perms, AESV3 DefaultCryptFilter, StmF/StrF valid — while the XRefStm dict carries the ORIGINAL `/Encrypt` indirect ref; same appended plaintext page n..n+3, `/Root` n, `/Prev` orig; not in prevchain VARIANTS) x 2 seeds x 6 engines = 12 no-password probes → ORIGINAL 0/12, injected 0/12 — ALL six engines refuse, 0 crashes. Verdicts: pypdf FileNotDecryptedError; pdfminer PDFPasswordIncorrect (derivation attempted); pymupdf FileDataError (same exception class as the cycle-33 baseline — the XRefStm original-ref changes nothing on the MuPDF path, unlike the cycle-63 reverse direction where MuPDF retreated to `ValueError: document closed or encrypted`); pypdfium2 Incorrect password; pikepdf PasswordError; pdfjs PasswordException/No password given. Verdict profile IDENTICAL to the cycle-33 direct-hostile-dict baseline on every stack — trailer-wins, fail-closed, everywhere. Structural-validity evidence (no positive with-password control possible by design — the trailer hostile dict cannot authenticate): 5/6 engines parse the file and refuse at the auth layer, and pikepdf/qpdf refuses EVEN WITH the correct user password on both files, proving the trailer dict governs for qpdf. Forty-sixth unanimous-refuse variant. Still integrity-only (LOG.md O-2026-002 extension). Builder + raw results: `/tmp/opencode/cycle64_hybrid_trailer_hostile.py`, `/tmp/opencode/cycle64_hostiletrailer/` (2 PDFs + results.json, git-untracked by location); no new repo files, no PoC (negative result).

## Leaks / crashes

- leaks: 0. No user-password content recoverable without password on any surface tested.
- crashes: 0.
- PoCs on file (observations, not leaks): unchanged from 2026-10-31.

- probes this day: 1 cycle x 12 = 12 no-password probes (2 seeds x 6 engines).

## Next step

- Hybrid-disagreement axis now mapped at both directions (XS-hostile cycle 63 / trailer-hostile cycle 64), both unanimous-refuse with trailer-wins resolution everywhere. Next smallest Track 2 steps: hybrid with hostile dict in BOTH trailer and XRefStm (agreeing-hostile control — do all six still refuse identically, or does agreement change the MuPDF FileDataError?); or hostile trailer dict + XRefStm with NO /Encrypt (trailer-only vs XS-absent split, mirrors the cycle-45 CF-absent isolation); or return to single-revision axis leftovers (indirect-ref hostile dict was cycle 62 — done; remaining: /Perms-zeroed-CF-absent split, CFM-AESV3-with-V4 cross-mismatch).
