- t_hostileBothXS (Track 2, cycle 65): NEW variant, agreeing-hostile control completing the hybrid-disagreement axis — BOTH the classic trailer AND the XRefStm dict carry the cycle-33 V5/R6 hostile DIRECT dict (zeroed O/U/OE/UE, zeroed Perms, AESV3 DefaultCryptFilter, StmF/StrF valid; same appended plaintext page n..n+3, `/Root` n, `/Prev` orig, `/XRefStm` ptr; not in prevchain VARIANTS) x 2 seeds x 6 engines = 12 no-password probes → ORIGINAL 0/12, injected 0/12 — ALL six engines refuse, 0 crashes. Verdict profile IDENTICAL to the trailer-hostile cycle-64 split on every stack, including pymupdf `FileDataError` (same class as the cycle-33 baseline — NOT the cycle-63 `ValueError` retreat): agreement changes nothing anywhere, the XRefStm dict is irrelevant once the trailer carries a hostile dict, so trailer-wins resolution is unconditional, not disagreement-dependent. With-password controls (correct user password): PyMuPDF cannot open either file even to authenticate (pre-auth FileDataError); pikepdf/qpdf refuses WITH the password, proving no fallback to the original-via-`/Prev` dict on any path. Forty-seventh unanimous-refuse variant. Still integrity-only (LOG.md O-2026-002 extension). Builder + raw results: `/tmp/opencode/cycle65_agreeing_hostile.py`, `/tmp/opencode/cycle65_hostileboth/` (2 PDFs + results.json, git-untracked by location); no new repo files, no PoC (negative result).

